text That's when she came to this school.
sound HRY.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text Together with me...
sound HRZ.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text After the accident, Rie-chan seemed so lifeless...
sound HS0.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text I tried really hard to cheer her up, but nothing worked...
sound HS1.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text It made me sad too.
sound HS2.aac
text @[Furukawa]
text ...
sound HS3.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text But then, one day, we met someone wonderful.
sound HS4.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text Our ancient literature teacher... Koumura-sensei.
sound HS5.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text Koumura-sensei taught Rie-chan how amazing music can be all over again.
sound HS6.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text He told her that even if she couldn't play an instrument, she could still make music.
sound HS7.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text And after he did, he began to sing...
sound HS8.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text Though his voice was hoarse and he wasn't always on tune... he was singing from the heart...
sound HS9.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text That song touched Rie-chan...
sound HSA.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text And she began to sing too.
sound HSB.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text When she did, she looked like the old, energetic Rie-chan.
sound HSC.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text After that, she started to want to show as many people as she could how wonderful singing can be.
sound HSD.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text That's why she wanted to make a choral club, something this school doesn't have.
sound HSE.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text ...Together with Koumura-sensei.
sound HSF.aac
text @[Sugisaka]
text I feel the same way.
text She wipes the tears that have begun to well in her eyes... and smiles as she talks.
text And then...
sound HSG.aac
